ry":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record here runs from 1951 to 2025, and on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 8 grids October to November came in under 90% of normal in 39 of those 75 years. In 2025 the middle of the grids got 20% of normal in November to December and 50% in July to August. This year started short, with January to February 2026 at 52% of normal on the middle. Every grid had its driest year in 1963, and grid 18456 got down to 60% that year.</p>"}
